seafile-server (14.0.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  An optional seafile-thumbnail-server package is now available. It
  generates thumbnails for more file types in the web interface. Install
  it, set ENABLE_THUMBNAIL_SERVER in /etc/seafile/seahub_settings.py,
  enable the /thumbnail/ route in the proxy and restart seafile.target:
  https://github.com/dionysius/seafile-deb/wiki/Configuration#thumbnail-server

  On Ubuntu, add the xtradeb PPA, pinned to Chromium, before installing
  it: https://github.com/dionysius/seafile-deb/wiki/Installation
  The PPA provides chromium-headless-shell, which Ubuntu doesn't ship as
  a deb package.

 -- dionysius <dragon.dionysius@gmail.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:24:42 +0100

seafile-server (14.0.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  Seafile 14.0 removes, renames and moves many configuration options. Review
  the changes offered for the files in /etc/seafile carefully instead of
  keeping the old versions.

